DESCRIPTION:Juneteenth marks June 19\, 1865 — the day Major General Gordo
 n Granger issued General Order No. 3 at Galveston\, informing the people o
 f Texas that all enslaved people were free. The Emancipation Proclamation 
 had taken effect two and a half years earlier\, and the distance between t
 hose two dates is the substance of the holiday: a freedom declared and a f
 reedom enforced are not the same thing. Texas made the day a legal state h
 oliday in 1980\; Congress added it to the federal holiday list in 2021.\n\
 nhttps://todaycelebrates.com/holiday/juneteenth/
